<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Associated Domains (ADR-029). TWO associations, claiming different, non-overlapping
  paths on two origins:
    - applinks:beanies.family     → the OAuth return Universal Link
                                    (https://beanies.family/oauth/native), matched by
                                    web/public/.well-known/apple-app-site-association.
    - applinks:app.beanies.family → shared links (/join, /welcome) and entity deep links
                                    (#63), matched by public/.well-known/apple-app-site-association.
                                    That file's path list is owned by
                                    src/constants/externalDeepLinkPaths.ts and pinned to it
                                    by src/constants/__tests__/deepLinkPaths.manifests.test.ts.
                                    It deliberately EXCLUDES /oauth/* — /oauth/callback on
                                    that origin is the Drive Picker's web return path.
  App Groups (#64): `group.family.beanies.app` is the ONLY channel between the Share
  Extension and the app — they are separate processes that share nothing else. The
  extension writes each shared document into this container; ShareIntentPlugin reads and
  CLEARS it when the app becomes active. The SAME group must be declared on the
  ShareExtension target's entitlements, and the identifier must be registered in the
  Developer portal (Identifiers → App Groups) before signing can resolve it.

  The former webcredentials:app.beanies.family (passkey) association was retired with
  the native WebAuthn-PRF pivot to the hardware Keystore (ADR-029, 2026-07-14) — native
  biometric no longer uses WebAuthn. Both AASA files now carry the real Apple Team ID
  (V2CKCNM3S7); the <APPLE_TEAM_ID> placeholder this comment used to warn about is gone
  from public/ and web/public/, and the claim that it was still there was stale — see
  docs/plans/2026-08-06-ios-oauth-custom-scheme-bridge.md:92, which identified it and
  never landed the fix. The remaining live steps are in the substitution checklist in
  docs/runbooks/native-store-submission.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:beanies.family</string>
		<string>applinks:app.beanies.family</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.family.beanies.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
